  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Decision\\n\\n**The global, filter-independent durable-position behaviour applies.** Under the pinned integration (`@ordarium/*` **1.3.1**), the observation/change-feed cursor is a single ledger-wide commit position — not a per-subscription position.\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n| Source | Authority | Says |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `node_modules/@ordarium/core/dist/src/types.d.ts` → `StateChangePage` | pinned published contract, `normativeStatus: normative`, `authorityDomain: ordarium-interface`, `versionScope: 1.3.1` | `cursor`: *\\\"Opaque, **filter-independent** durable position of the last delivered change.\\\"* `StateChangeFilter.namespace` only *\\\"restrict[s] observation\\\"* to a namespace |\\n| `node_modules/@ordarium/ledger-sqlite/dist/src/index.js` `changes()` | shipped implementation of that contract | `ordarium_state_changes (change_seq INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT)` is one global sequence; the comment states *\\\"the cursor is a **global, filter-independent position**, so this compares against the whole ledger, not the requested namespace's last sequence.\\\"* Cursor = last delivered `change_seq`; namespace filter only narrows rows |\\n| `.../migrations.js` | shipped implementation | v3→v4 b",
